# Copy to .env (gitignored) next to docker-compose.yml; `docker compose` (and so `pnpm stack:up`)
# reads it. Never commit real values. Restart the stack after a change: `pnpm stack:up`.

# Google sign-in, optional. Leave these unset and the API runs without it (the app says so and
# the dev login keeps working). Set all four or none. Step by step: docs/google-sign-in.md.
#
# The OAuth client (type "Web application") from the Google Cloud Console:
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=1234567890-abcdefg.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-your-client-secret
#
# The API's callback, exactly as registered with the client: your machine's Tailscale https name
# (tailnet only, through `tailscale serve`), or http://localhost:3000/... for the browser target.
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://your-machine.your-tailnet.ts.net/auth/google/callback
#
# Where the API may send the browser back to the app, comma separated: Expo Go on the phone
# (exp://<tailscale ip>:8081) and the web target (http://localhost:8081).
# GOOGLE_APP_RETURN_URLS=exp://100.64.0.1:8081,http://localhost:8081

# Push notifications, optional. Unset, the API sends nothing and only records the development
# outbox. PUSH_SENDER=expo sends through Expo's push service (the API needs outbound internet,
# not a public address). Step by step: docs/push-notifications.md.
# PUSH_SENDER=expo
# Only if the Expo project turned on "enhanced security for push notifications":
# EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN=
